Fixed against Python (ENG-6): a private key whose lines are separate items of a list or values of a dict.
ferb/sanitize/redact.py left a key body unredacted when it sat under a non-text key, in a nested list or in
bytes between the BEGIN and END items, read no node's text as a key line, and in a dict never looked for a
key when no value was a short text with a digit; it masked a bare boolean between the lines. With this patch
every text, integer and byte string from the BEGIN item to the END item is masked at any depth (keys and shape
kept); booleans, None and floats stay. Same behavior as rust/crates/ferb-sanitize (redact.rs key_item).
Apply from the repository root: git apply rust/fixtures/sanitize/python-redact-fix.patch

